    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d301">

                <pb facs="0264" n="254" xml:id="pg254"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/4–2049: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister-Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Clark</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canton</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-04-20T09:00:00+08:00">April 20, 1949—9
                            a. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 20—6:16 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Cantel 241. George Yeh, Acting Foreign Minister, said that when Li Tsung-jen at
                    Canton he was accused at meeting CEC of having eventual intention to sell out to
                    Communists. Li had insisted he was no coward; had no intention of surrendering,
                    and pled with those present not to prejudge him but to await his actions. Yeh is
                    convinced Li will not accept Communist ultimatum and that fighting will be
                    resumed, but he anticipates reshuffle in Cabinet. Of prime importance is to
                    obtain leader who can hold military together in some semblance unified command
                    and Ho Ying-chin seems only one available. Yeh said there has been talk of
                    making Ho Supreme Commander in Chief, but Ho continues refuse. Yeh thinks,
                    therefore, Ho will remain Premier and may assume tasks if suitable Commander in
                    Chief unfound.</p>
                <p>Sent Department Cantel 241; repeated Nanking 206, Shanghai 159.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clark</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
